<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haldi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khaldi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haldi was the chief god of Urartu, a warrior deity at the head of a pantheon that also included the storm god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teisheba">Teisheba</a> and the sun god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivini">Shivini</a>. Urartian kings attributed their victories to him and opened their inscriptions with his name. His most famous temple stood at Musasir, which was sacked by the Assyrian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> in 714 BCE.</p></div>
